  "body": "**Replaces #440**, which was opened from the old fork. GitHub detached that fork from this repo's network when NeoTech/Camcraft was briefly private, so #440 can no longer be updated. **Now stacked on #471** (the replacement for #439).\n\n(Originally stacked on #439.) The #438 work is 9d9ac93d.\n\n## What changed\n- **The tool-number clash check (#221) is judged per machine.** `tool_numbers::clash_per_machine` runs the existing `clash()` on each machine group from `program_mounts(world, false)`. `posting::op_streams` calls it, which covers per-op files too.\n- **Why per machine, not per NC file:** a T number names a pocket in one machine's tool changer.\n  - Two machines have two tool tables, so T2 on each is fine.\n  - Two posts on one machine still load from one carousel, so a shared number there is still refused.\n  - Grouping per file (machine plus post) would let that real clash through, so I rejected it.\n- **Messages:** a single-machine program gets the exact #221 message, unchanged. A multi-machine refusal starts with the mount's label (`Setup1 (machine, post): tools '…' and '…' would both post as T3 …`).\n- The rationale is in `docs/decisions/388-per-setup-mount.md` (#438 section).\n\n## How tested\n- New `setup_mounts_post::a_tool_number_shared_across_machines_posts_but_clashes_within_one`:\n  - across machines: a mill tool numbered 2 and the lathe's T2 post as two files;\n  - within one machine: a clash is refused, naming both tools, the T number and Setup1, and not the lathe tool.\n- `tool_numbers::two_tools_posting_one_number_refuse_by_name` (single machine) is unchanged and passes.\n- `setup_mounts_post` 6/6, `setup_mount` 6/6, `tool_numbers` 6/6, `posting` 17/17, `post_not_judged` 4/4. `clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\nChangelog: The tool-number clash is judged per machine, so two machines in one program may each use the same T number (#438)\n\nFixes #438\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
